const PRIVACY := "Adventure Odyssey Privacy Policy\nDraft for review | Current title-screen preview | October 17, 2026\n\nDeveloper: Dabsky\nPrivacy and support: dabskycreativestudio@gmail.com\n\nAbout this preview\nThis notice describes the Adventure Odyssey title-screen preview. The preview displays artwork, animations and sample account forms. It does not create an account, connect to Google or open a playable game world.\n\nInformation you type\nThe email, password and confirmation fields process your entries locally to demonstrate the form and check its format. Use made-up details, never a real password. The preview's app code does not send these entries to Dabsky or another service, log them, or save them to an account database or file.\n\nClearing entries\nYour entries remain in the open form until you change them, successfully complete its local validation, or close the form. Invalid entries remain so you can correct them. Successful validation and closing clear the fields. This is normal interface clearing, not a guarantee of forensic erasure from device memory or third-party keyboards.\n\nOther data and services\nThe current app code has no advertising, analytics, purchases, cloud saves, account identifiers or location collection. No account or analytics provider is integrated. The Android export configuration disables internet access. The app does not sell or share demonstration entries or use them for targeted advertising.\n\nYour device, keyboard, operating system and download platform can process information under their own policies. This notice does not describe or control their independent practices.\n\nQuestions and requests\nThere is no Adventure Odyssey account or server-side account record to delete in this preview. Close the form to clear its entries. You can send questions to dabskycreativestudio@gmail.com. Emailing that address sends your email address and message to the support mailbox. Do not send passwords or other sensitive information.\n\nBefore future online features\nAccount services and other data-using features require a new review and an updated privacy notice describing their actual practices before they are enabled. This draft does not describe a future account service. The developer's legal identity, support-message retention and applicable audience-specific requirements remain under review; this is not a final adopted policy.\n"
